Homepage: https://www.retroarch.com/
Description: frontend for libretro API-compatible applications
 RetroArch is an open source, multi-platform frontend for emulators and
 standalone games that are compatible with the libretro API, which it refers to
 as "cores." Depending on the available cores, it can be used as a modular
 multi-emulator system, game engine, media player or merely a 3-D technical
 demonstration.
 .
 A large number of the popular hardware emulators which drive the moderm
 retro-gaming movement have been adapted into freely available libretro cores,
 to which RetroArch can then add sophisticated features such as: dynamic rate
 control, audio filters, multi-pass video shaders, netplay, gameplay rewinding
 and cheats. Libretro cores also share a standardized set of configuration
 options, saving users the need to manually configure each one prior to use.
 .
 This package provides all four RetroArch menu drivers, each offering a unique
 "flavor" of graphical user interface.
   - Ozone (the modern default, modelled after the Nintendo Switch UI)
   - XMB (Ozone's predecessor, based on Sony's Playstation 3 and PSP UIs)
   - GLUI (for touchscreen devices, following Google's Material UI principles)
   - RGUI (for low-power and/or low-resolution devices)

